WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.810 --> 00:02.950
Imagine a skill acquisition spectrum

2
00:03.650 --> 00:05.670
which spans from being a complete novice

3
00:06.410 --> 00:07.650
to the point of true mastery.

4
00:09.130 --> 00:11.390
When you encounter a new task or challenge,

5
00:11.850 --> 00:13.440
something you don't know how to tackle yet,

6
00:14.050 --> 00:15.490
first set a learning intention.

7
00:16.870 --> 00:17.630
For example,

8
00:18.210 --> 00:20.640
to experiment with a new project management tool,

9
00:21.770 --> 00:23.460
or even learn to play a new instrument.

10
00:24.390 --> 00:28.190
In these early stages of learning,
you shouldn't fixate on how well you're doing.

11
00:29.000 --> 00:31.360
Instead, focus on the quality of your learning.

12
00:32.810 --> 00:34.630
When you decide to take up a new skill,

13
00:35.080 --> 00:37.790
you may set performance goals too early in the process,

14
00:38.530 --> 00:41.860
and when you fail to achieve them,
you feel overwhelmed and even give up.

15
00:42.690 --> 00:44.070
But don't fall into that trap.

16
00:47.000 --> 00:48.400
Meet Paula.

17
00:48.580 --> 00:50.050
She loves playing the piano,

18
00:50.440 --> 00:52.930
and her dream is to play a piece with her friends.

19
00:54.600 --> 00:56.190
So she sets a learning intention:

20
00:57.160 --> 01:00.770
learn how to play the piano so that she can
begin learning a piece with her friend,

21
01:01.570 --> 01:06.530
because before she can consider setting a performance goal,
like performing with her friends in front of guests,

22
01:08.170 --> 01:14.880
she will need to practice with purpose and focus in order to develop
the dexterity and speed required to play the piano.

23
01:16.970 --> 01:20.350
Once you practice sufficiently
and continue to develop your skills,

24
01:20.970 --> 01:23.940
you can then apply your learning
and introduce performance goals.

25
01:24.740 --> 01:29.190
In the workplace, the distinction between setting
a learning intention and a performance goal

26
01:29.670 --> 01:30.980
would look something like this.

27
01:31.780 --> 01:35.360
“Increase sales revenue by 10% this year”
is a performance goal.

28
01:36.170 --> 01:39.970
It's not something you would set unless
you were already competent in your sales skills.

29
01:41.450 --> 01:43.870
This is where starting with a learning intention would help.

30
01:44.840 --> 01:45.630
For example,

31
01:45.990 --> 01:49.790
taking the time to deepen your expertise
about one of your company's new offerings,

32
01:50.440 --> 01:53.380
or practicing your customer talking points with colleagues.

33
01:54.250 --> 01:59.110
With that solid foundation, you'll be equipped
to eventually meet the challenge of a performance goal.

34
02:00.770 --> 02:03.840
Whether it's learning to play the piano
or something much simpler,

35
02:04.650 --> 02:08.640
you'll know you are ready to perform when you feel
excited to demonstrate what you've learned.

36
02:09.890 --> 02:12.960
And if you find yourself somewhere
in between on the learning spectrum,

37
02:13.320 --> 02:16.510
you can set a mix of learning intentions
and performance goals.

38
02:17.320 --> 02:18.980
In our rapidly changing world,

39
02:19.460 --> 02:22.370
there is an increasing number of opportunities to grow and learn.

40
02:23.690 --> 02:29.030
Whether you find yourself exploring new roles or taking on
new responsibilities as part of your existing role,

41
02:29.830 --> 02:35.110
you will set yourself up for long-term performance and success
when you start by setting learning intentions.
